Local fixes that let stock PW4 5.13.6 reach Home in katadelos/eink-emulator 8e1e42e.
devloop/emulator/setup.sh applies this with git apply.

Upstream: https://github.com/katadelos/eink-emulator @8e1e42e, which carries
no licence. This patch is ours; it is kept to the changed lines plus one line
of context each, so it reproduces as little of the upstream code as possible.

- models.json: the Rex machine's default IDME board_id, 00015R0000000000, is a
  legacy tattoo ID that /etc/upstart/functions decodes as platform=yoshi. The
  guest then stays on the boot splash and never starts USB SSH. Use the PSN v2
  form with the moonshine code 15R.
- guest-overrides/rex: kb crashes when it loads its second keyboard plugin at
  the address of the first one under QEMU. Three crashes make lab126_gui
  reboot the guest. Expose only the device-language plugin.

diff --git a/eink_emulator/images/rootfs.py b/eink_emulator/images/rootfs.py
index a9945c0..2219967 100644
--- a/eink_emulator/images/rootfs.py
+++ b/eink_emulator/images/rootfs.py
@@ -577,2 +577,6 @@ def prepare_rex(source: Path, output: Path) -> None:
         "/etc/upstart/qemu-seed-locale.conf": ("qemu-seed-locale.conf", "0100644"),
+        "/etc/upstart/qemu-keyboard-single-language.conf": (
+            "qemu-keyboard-single-language.conf",
+            "0100644",
+        ),
     })
diff --git a/guest-overrides/rex/qemu-keyboard-single-language.conf b/guest-overrides/rex/qemu-keyboard-single-language.conf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d27d972
--- /dev/null
+++ b/guest-overrides/rex/qemu-keyboard-single-language.conf
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# kb probes every keyboard plugin by loading and unloading
+# /usr/share/keyboard/<language>/utils.so in turn. Each plugin reuses the
+# address range of the previous one, and under QEMU the second plugin then
+# crashes kb with SIGSEGV or SIGABRT. Three crashes make lab126_gui reboot the
+# device. Expose only the plugin for the device language so that kb loads a
+# single plugin. Other on-screen keyboard languages are unavailable.
+
+start on starting kb
+
+task
+
+script
+    if grep -q ' /usr/share/keyboard tmpfs ' /proc/mounts; then
+        exit 0
+    fi
+    lang=en_US
+    if [ -s /var/local/system/locale ]; then
+        lang=$(awk -F'[=.]' '/^LANG=/{print $2}' /var/local/system/locale)
+    fi
+    [ -f "/usr/share/keyboard/$lang/utils.so" ] || lang=en_US
+    dir=/var/tmp/qemu-keyboard
+    mkdir -p "$dir"
+    cp -a "/usr/share/keyboard/$lang" /usr/share/keyboard/images "$dir/"
+    for entry in /usr/share/keyboard/*; do
+        [ -d "$entry" ] || cp -a "$entry" "$dir/"
+    done
+    mount --bind "$dir" /usr/share/keyboard
+    echo "Exposed only the $lang keyboard plugin for QEMU" > /dev/console || true
+end script
diff --git a/models.json b/models.json
index cf9f0b2..2f5545e 100644
--- a/models.json
+++ b/models.json
@@ -726,2 +726,5 @@
       "falcon_bios": ["bios.bin"]
+    },
+    "machine_properties": {
+      "idme-pcbsn": "P0015R0000000000"
     }
